          "kicker": "Rankings race",
          "heading": "Wallabies could knock England out of fifth with Sydney Bledisloe win",
          "body": "England's grip on fifth in the World Rugby rankings is under threat from Australia, who were beaten 50-19 by New Zealand at Eden Park last weekend. Planet Rugby's projections, based on the table as of 16 October, have England on 85.68 and Australia on 84.89. A Wallabies win over the All Blacks in Sydney's second Bledisloe Test would lift Australia, coached by Les Kiss, above England, and a margin of more than 15 points would put them fourth, ahead of France."
