          "heading": "Len Ikitau out with concussion as Declan Meredith starts at 10",
          "body": "Wallabies coach Les Kiss has been forced into a reshuffle for Australia's second Bledisloe Cup Test against New Zealand at Accor Stadium. Wallaby Len Ikitau is out with a concussion and Ben Donaldson was hurt in the build-up, so Declan Meredith starts at fly-half and Joseph-Aukuso Sua'ali'i moves back into the centres, with Harry Potter coming into the midfield. Ewen McKenzie, the former Wallabies head coach, said on the Rugby Unity podcast that Kiss' \"hands have been forced\", while admitting he was still baffled by some of the calls."
